{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the non-convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> shown below, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/23386faeefe37629243fa264877b288499db5048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is a right angle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd17cd296404d0c6d0a3c231fdb77597e9e9348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746fe6b6679f693c884c68a86c6dabd02ee2c299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff2219e4b6351e8b0b3b3ba2294a9133e4bf38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. What is the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be32bf473ea4532b8cc3eb844835e13b70bbfba9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)--(2.4,3.6)--(0,5)--(12,0)--(0,0)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (0, 0), SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (12, 0), ESE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (2.4, 3.6), SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (0, 5), N);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d6144d3482981556caa261a88c0d0345bc9062cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }12 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }24 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }26 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }30 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first connect point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66f241a2e30d6733c30bc1e3c4236af99f628ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]draw((0,0)--(2.4,3.6)--(0,5)--(12,0)--(0,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,5)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (0, 0), SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (12, 0), ESE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, (2.4, 3.6), SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (0, 5), N);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"128\" /> \n</p><p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is a 3-4-5 right triangle. We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae57734732e77d0de15f999bd1f4f9ee814d8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDA$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, by the 5-12-13 Pythagorean triple. With these lengths, we can solve the problem. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae57734732e77d0de15f999bd1f4f9ee814d8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDA$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a7676fa540fa7a49121c32ec0c926dc78fd023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\cdot 12}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"37\" />, and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67af5e69ca5cd7d3883db2b345ee2cab700b1b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\cdot 4}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/17349e82f19ff0b9193d24284ed1288b7b61b3e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 24}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"140\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is a 3-4-5 right triangle. So the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is 6. Then we can use Heron's formula to compute the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> whose sides have lengths 5,12,and 13. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea86df191425a6f9121a6a3832a08f1c12ded0d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{s(s-5)(s-12)(s-13)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"207\" height=\"32\" /> , where s is the semi-perimeter of the triangle, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b553f2a38d8046852e05a359b5eb772eec33d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=(5+12+13)/2=15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is 30, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/17349e82f19ff0b9193d24284ed1288b7b61b3e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 24}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"140\" height=\"28\" /> ---LarryFlora\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aH4GrC5Nfwk?si=tFdEHOoFbkp4q7tD\">https://youtu.be/aH4GrC5Nfwk?si=tFdEHOoFbkp4q7tD</a>\n</p><p>~ savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-e